In article <1skq9iINN481@news.u.washington.edu>, lazuli@u.washington.edu (Fred Sloniker) writes:
> [...]
> * What the heck are shriekers, anyway?  They don't do damage, they don't
>   kill attributes... do they curse or something?

They wake up everybody on the level.  Occasionally this is bad:
in my last game, Dr. Utah Jake found a throne room full of sleeping
monsters.  He wanted to save them for the next altar he found, which
was conveniently located one floor down.  But while converting the
altar, a large congregation came in to pray and didn't like the 
changes.  Utah kept running down the stairs, taking a few hacks and
running back up to rest, when suddenly a Shreiker appeared at the
top of the stairs.  I knew he was killing the congregation too slowly
to do much sacrificing, but I had hopes for the court.  The shreiker
dashed these, however, and a rather grumpy herd cut him off before he
could make for the exit.

He didn't beat his previous score.
